<BaseLayout title="Ecosystem" description="How PlayMAKER's website, tagging, graphics and video tools exchange data as development progresses." path="/ecosystem/">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">The ecosystem</p><h1>One club.<br />Many ways to play.</h1><p class="section-lede">The tools are modular. Connections between them are being designed, and the full workflow is not yet available.</p></div></section>
  <section class="page-section"><div class="shell"><div class="content-grid"><div class="panel"><p class="section-kicker">01 / Publish</p><h2>WebMAKER</h2><p>Studio 0.2 creates basketball or football club sites, can publish a public GitHub repository and enables the included Pages workflow.</p></div><div class="panel"><p class="section-kicker">02 / Capture</p><h2>TagMAKER</h2><p>The 0.1 source alpha tags basketball and football footage, imports WebMAKER rosters, exports player-statistics CSV and publishes versioned JSON.</p></div><div class="panel"><p class="section-kicker">03 / Design</p><h2>PostMAKER</h2><p>The 0.3 PWA and Windows app import public WebMAKER data and create post, story and square PNG graphics using reusable club assets.</p></div><div class="panel"><p class="section-kicker">04 / Edit</p><h2>VideoMAKER</h2><p>Guided match editing and import of TagMAKER data are planned. The application is still in early development.</p></div><div class="panel"><p class="section-kicker">Interoperability</p><h2>Data should travel</h2><p>The <a class="inline-link" href="https://github.com/PlayMAKER-apps/playmaker-schema" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">shared schema</a> documents public club data and TagMAKER JSON contracts. Stored format changes require explicit compatibility guidance and migrations.</p></div></div><div class="callout"><p><strong>Current compatibility:</strong> WebMAKER shares roster paths with TagMAKER and public club data with PostMAKER. VideoMAKER integration remains planned. Each released product also works independently.</p></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
